-- Wandering Isle (map 860): ambient wildlife and birds walk patrol paths instead of standing in place / wandering at random.
-- What a player sees today: 35 spawns (Pei-Wu Tiger x3, Emerald Singer x2, Mottled Rabbit x3, Long-Eared Mink x6, Mossback Toad x17, Corsac Fox x2, Whitefeather Crane x1, Softshell Turtle x1) move randomly inside a small radius around
--   their spawn point; in the reference data the same spawns follow a fixed walking route.
-- Cause: the routes (waypoint paths) were never imported; the spawns only have MovementType 1 (random movement).
-- Checked: every spawn is matched to a reference spawn of the same creature entry within 5 yards; every route has at least 3 points,
--   its nearest point lies within 6 yards of the spawn and its longest span is at most 60 yards. None of the spawns has a script name,
--   a per-guid smart script, a formation, a pool, a game event, a mount, a stand state or emote, a waypoint or a creature_addon path;
--   the smart scripts of the entries only cast spells in combat. Waypoint ids and addon path_id follow the local convention path_id = spawn guid.
-- Change: creature_addon.path_id = guid, waypoint_data rows (points renumbered from 1, walking, no delay) and MovementType 2 / wander_distance 0.
-- Source: LegionCore 7.3.5 world database (GPL2), table waypoint_data joined to its creature spawns on map 860; the SkyFire 5.4.8 database
--   has no routes for these spawns. Reviewed 18-11-2026.
-- Rollback (restores the previous movement of these spawns and removes the routes):
